          "metadata": {
            "name": "Label Data Extraction Node"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773442992079"
          },
          "code": "LABEL_DATA_EXTRACTION_NODE",
          "id": "1773442166390",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773442166391_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intelligent data-extraction assistant.\n\nUser Sentence can be taken from \n\nUser Chat Window:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n##Email Sender Input\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ReportsFromEmail}}\n\n##Email Send To Input\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.EmailSendTo}}\n\n----\nYour task:\n\nRead the user's sentence describing one or more report execution requests.\n\nIf multiple report requests are present, split them into separate requests.\n\nFor each request, identify whether the request asks for a label and ignore any other requests.\n\nParameter extraction rules (fully generic):\n\nAny phrase in the sentence that looks like a parameter assignment (e.g., \"X Y Z Value,\" \"X as Value,\" \"X = Value\") should be treated as a key-value pair.\n\nThe first contiguous words before the value are the parameter key.\n\nThe words after the key (until the next parameter or end of sentence) are the parameter value.\n\nUse the Report Name given by the User Sentence to find each key's official name. There are several possible Report Names (Item Label, Serial Label,Lot Label,Location Label, Receipt Delivery Label,LPN Label,LPN Content Label). Only capture report information for these Label reports. Any other document requests should be ignored along with their parameters.\n\nOnly use the ESS Parameters under its dedicated Report Name. Do not Use ESS Parameters from another report that is not requested.\n\nEvery Label Document Object should have the following keys hardcoded keys.\n\nReceipt\nShipment\nOrganization\nAssociated\nOnhand\nSubinventory\nLocator\nZone\nPrinter\nEmailToAddress\n\n\nReturn the extracted results as a JSON collection.\n\n\nRules:\n\nAlways include \"Report Name\" in every request object.\n\nAlways include \"Report Number\" which is sequential starting at \"1\" for the first request, \"2\" for the second, and so on.\n\nExtract only parameters explicitly mentioned by the user that fall under the hardcoded parameter keys.\n\nDo NOT invent or infer missing values.\n\nIf Email Send To Input is empty or null do not set a value for EmailToAddress. Do not set EmailToAddress to the value of the input Email Sender Input that is completely different and should never be used to set EmailToAddress.\n\n\nAssociated can be found in user sentences when they mention it with a specific subinventory or locator. Look for requests that look like \"Retrieve item labels for items associated with subinventory stores and locator 00.\" In that example note that the report is Item Label and we set associated to true as the requests wants items associated to subinventories and locators. If association to a subinventory or locator is not mentioned set the value as false.\n\nOnhand can be found in user sentences when they mention it with a specific subinventory or locator. Look for requests that look like \"Retrieve item labels for items with onhand in subinventory stores and locator 00.\" In that example note that the report is Item Label and we set Onhand to true as the requests wants items with onhand in a specific subinventories or locators. If onhand in a subinventory or locator is not mentioned set the value as false.\n\nPreserve exact values for codes, numbers, and IDs.\n\nIf the input message does not mention an email to send to, then check if the Email Send To Input is populated and set the value as the EmailToAddress.\n\nOutput format requirements:\n\nOutput ONLY valid JSON\n\nThe top-level output must be a JSON object\n\nEach key value must be in a JSON object\n\nEach object must contain key-value pairs for \"Report Name\", \"Report Number\", and the explicitly mentioned hard coded key parameters\n\nNo extra text, no explanations, no markdown\n\nIf a parameter is not mentioned in the User Sentence then set the value for the hardcoded key as null\n\n----Examples:\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get a Transfer Order Report for Receipt 1298 with Requisition BU Vision Operations and Subinventory Stores.\n\nExample Output:\n\n{}\n\nExplanation: The reason why the Output is Empty and doesn't return anything even though there is a Receipt and Subinventory Parameter which we are looking for from the hardcoded list, the request is for a Transfer Order Report and we are specifically looking for Label reports. \n\n\nExample Input:\nRun Label Report for Shipment Chowder, and Item AS54888.\n\nExample Output:\n\n{}\n\nExplanation: Even though this example is for a Label Report it doesn't specify the specific Label Report therefore we return an empty object.\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get an item label for Shipment 88971ST and organization V1.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"ReportNumber\": \"1\",\n  \"ReportName\":\"Item Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\":\"88971ST\",\n  \"Organization\": \"V1\",\n  \"Associated\": false,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\":null,\n   \"Locator\":null,\n    \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":null,\n   \"EmailToAddress\":null\n}\n\nExplanation: This time the input requests an item label which falls under the Label report names we can use. Then we look if any of our hardcoded parameters can be included in this report. Shipment is mentioned so we set the value for that key.\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get an item label for items in Subinventory XMLP and Locator '1.1.1.' and in Organization XYz.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"Report Number\": \"1\",\n  \"Report Name\":\"Item Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\":null,\n  \"Organization\": \"XYz\",\n  \"Associated\":true,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\":\"XMLP\",\n   \"Locator\":\"1.1.1.\",\n   \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":null,\n   \"EmailToAddress\":null\n}\n\nExplanation: This time the input requests an item label which falls under the Label report names we can use. Then we look if any of our hardcoded parameters can be included in this report. Subinventory is given by the input. Notice the locator is in between single quotes indicating that the value is everything in between including the ending period for 1.1.1. also note that for the organization XYz is captured but this time we ignore the ending period as it is the end of the sentence. Ensure that when single quotes are given to include everything in between them such as periods, leading or ending spaces, and more as the value. Because they are asking for items in the subinventory we are assuming they mean associated. If they flat out mention onhand then associated would have been false and onhand true. Both Associated and Onhand can not be true at the same time. It's one or the other. The input must mention Onhand for it to be true. \n\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get an lot label for items in Subinventory JOJO and Locator '1.1.1.' and in Organization Beven and use Printer HPPackard.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"Report Number\": \"1\",\n  \"Report Name\":\"Lot Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\": null,\n  \"Organization\": \"Beven\",\n  \"Associated\":true,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\":\"JOJO\",\n   \"Locator\":\"1.1.1.\",\n   \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":\"HPPackard\",\n   \"EmailToAddress\":null\n}\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get an lpn label for items in Subinventory PLAT and Locator 'Y 1.1.1.' and in Organization Beven and use Email to lily@smithtires.com.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"Report Number\": \"1\",\n  \"Report Name\":\"LPN Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\": null,\n  \"Organization\": \"Beven\",\n  \"Associated\":true,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\":\"PLAT\",\n   \"Locator\":\"Y 1.1.1.\",\n   \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":null,\n   \"EmailToAddress\":\"lily@smithtires.com\"\n}\n\nExplanation: In this example notice how they mentioned the email address to send the request to. So we populate that value.\n\n\nExample Input:\nCan I get an lpn label for items in Subinventory PLAT and Locator 'Y 1.1.1.' and in Organization Beven and Email Koko@bestvans.com.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"Report Number\": \"1\",\n  \"Report Name\":\"LPN Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\": null,\n  \"Organization\": \"Beven\",\n  \"Associated\":true,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\":\"PLAT\",\n   \"Locator\":\"Y 1.1.1.\",\n   \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":null,\n   \"EmailToAddress\":\"Koko@bestvans.com\"\n}\n\nExplanation: Note that this time it mentions email Koko so that's who we are sending the email to and its from Sam so that is our Email from. \n\nExample Input:\nCan I get a lpn label for all subinventories and locators in organization Beven use email to blob@oracle.com.\n\nExample Output:\n\n\n{\n  \"Report Number\": \"1\",\n  \"Report Name\":\"LPN Label\",\n  \"Receipt\": null,\n  \"Shipment\": null,\n  \"Organization\": \"Beven\",\n  \"Associated\":false,\n  \"Onhand\":false,\n  \"Subinventory\": null,\n   \"Locator\": null,\n   \"Zone\":null,\n   \"Printer\":null,\n   \"EmailToAddress\":\"blob@bestvans.com\"\n}\n\nExplanation: Note in this example even thought the request is for subinventories and locatores because they did not specify a subinventory and locator we set those values as null. We set the report name and the email to the values provided.\n\n----End Examples\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"ReportNumber\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"ReportName\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Receipt\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Shipment\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Organization\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Associated\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"Onhand\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"Subinventory\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Locator\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Zone\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    },\n    \"Printer\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"minLength\": 1\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"ReportNumber\",\n    \"ReportName\",\n    \"Receipt\",\n    \"Shipment\",\n    \"Organization\",\n    \"Associated\",\n    \"Onhand\",\n    \"Subinventory\",\n    \"Locator\",\n    \"Zone\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
